a failed check ends a run that reaches its end with status 1: true
the handlers registered before Verdict's still run at a failing end: true
an exception escaping after a failed check is still reported: true
a run an exception ended says it stopped early: true
a run an exception ended still counts its failed checks: true
a run an exception ended exits with the runtime's status 2: true
the handlers registered before Verdict's still run when it stops early: true
nothing after the escaping exception ran: true
an exception in a run with no failed check is reported as the runtime reports it: true
an explicit exit 0 after a failed check exits 1: true
a catch-all that swallows the exit still ends the run with status 1: true
a case that raises is a failed claim naming the case and the exception: true
the case after a raising case still runs: true
an exit inside a case ends the run rather than failing the case: true
an exit inside a case after a failed check says which case stopped the run: true
every line of a multi-line failure carries the FAIL prefix: true
a run with three failed checks names all three on its last stderr line: true
a run with more failed checks than the line shows names the first ones, cut and on one line, and counts the rest: true
a claim whose computed label carries line breaks reports on one line of each stream: true
a failing run omits the success trailer it prints only when no claim failed: true
a failed pass_fail claim's stderr line is its stdout row behind FAIL:, bare or detailed: true
a case that returns prints only what its claims print: true

